# Who reviews what. GitHub automatically requests a review from the owner
# when a PR touches their files.
#
# ⚠️ These are GitHub handles, not the names shown in commits: the two often
# differ. A wrong handle raises no error, the line is just ignored - the file
# fails silently. To check a handle exists, open https://github.com/<handle>.
#
# GitHub only requests an owner's review if they have write access to the
# repository. Someone outside the organization will never be asked.
#
# The last rule matching a file wins: general patterns go at the top,
# specific cases at the bottom.

